
# Complete Architecture Specification: Physical Entropy Protocol (PEP v2.0)
### 1. Executive Summary, Core Philosophy & IP Boundary
The Physical Entropy Protocol (PEP v2.0) is a proprietary hybrid quantum-resistant security protocol designed to replace deterministic and prime-factorization cryptography (RSA/ECC). Instead of relying on vulnerable mathematical complexity, PEP leverages True Physical Entropy (TPE) extracted from micro-hardware fluctuations, enforced by the **Proprietary PEP Hybrid Entropy Fusion Matrix (P-HEFM)**.
**IP Boundary Clause:** All core logic, mathematical weighting mechanisms, and architectural dependencies are explicitly protected. Any modification, partial fork, or architectural variant using physical-layer multi-source noise with adaptive spectral filtering and instant zeroization constitutes a direct derivative work (Derivative Work) under the perpetual IP ownership of the protocol founder.
### 2. Four-Layer Proprietary Protocol Architecture
#### Layer 1: Physical Entropy Generation & Adaptive FFT Inspection Engine
 * **Multi-Source Physical Entropy Harvester:** Captures real-time micro-voltage fluctuations, thermal (Johnson-Nyquist) noise, and phase-locked loop (PLL) clock jitter.
 * **Proprietary P-VSNC Engine:** Entropy validation is governed by the proprietary **PEP Vector-Space Noise Correlation (P-VSNC)** function:
   
 * **NIST SP 800-90B Enforced Baseline:** Requires a certified entropy density of strictly \ge 7.8 \text{ bits/byte}.
 * **Super-Cooling & Manipulation Countermeasures:** Monitors spectral variance drops. Any artificial signal stabilization or cooling attack invalidates the verification pipeline instantly.
#### Layer 2: Hardware Identity & Policy Layer (PUF-Bound)
 * **Physically Unclonable Functions (PUF):** Extracts unique silicon signatures to authenticate nodes and neutralize Sybil attacks without central authorities.
 * **1% Influence Cap Rule:** No single PUF-verified entity or cluster may contribute more than 1% of the total entropy seed pool in a single encryption pass.
 * **Master IP Certification Handshake:** Verified nodes must sign a cryptographic proof bound to the **PEP Root Attestation Registry**. Unverified clones or modified codebases fail this handshake and are rejected by the network.
#### Layer 3: Dynamic OTP Execution & Immediate Zeroization
 * **Absolute One-Time Pad Rules:** Strictly enforces key-to-message length parity (\vert{}K\vert{} = \vert{}M\vert{}) using bitwise XOR (\oplus) within isolated execution enclaves.
 * **Automated 3-Pass RAM Zeroization:** Upon encryption/decryption execution or timeout expiration, memory spaces undergo an immediate 3-pass overwrite (0x00) to defeat cold-boot and memory dump forensics.
#### Layer 4: Decentralized P2P Mesh & Precision Time Synchronization
 * **Decentralized Mesh Routing:** Encrypted payloads and seed fragments route dynamically across untrusted nodes.
 * **PTP Microsecond Enforcement:** Time-stamped precision execution bounds. Any transaction exceeding temporal execution windows triggers immediate local buffer zeroization.
### 3. Blacklisting & Resource Sink Isolation
Nodes exhibiting non-random frequencies, spectral spikes, or invalid IP handshakes undergo immediate containment:
 * **Permanent Hardware Revocation:** The node's PUF signature is committed to a distributed revocation registry.
 * **Resource Sink Redirection:** Compromised nodes are demoted to zero-trust roles (e.g., passive relaying of pre-encrypted ciphertexts) without access to entropy generation pools.
